From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:37:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: install SCS and MSCS rules that the AP configures

EasyMesh 6.1 section 20.2.4 has a Multi-AP Agent activate MSCS and SCS
rules that its Controller sends for a station, also for a station that
sits behind the 4-address backhaul station of another agent. Such a rule
is not requested by the peer: the agent identifies it by the QMID of the
Controller and picks the SCSID itself, and the rule does not depend on
the association of the station with the agent's fronthaul AP.

Add hostapd_robust_av_configure(): it takes a whole SCS Descriptor or
MSCS Descriptor element for an associated peer and, where given, a host
behind it, and passes the rule to the driver with that client address,
an MSCS also with the configured flag. hostapd keeps no state of such a
rule and sends no frame and no robust-av notification for it. The
disallow lists and robust_av_scs_disabled apply to the requests of
stations only.

The element parsers of the request paths become scs_desc_elems_parse()
and mscs_desc_parse(), which both paths use.

DEL_MSCS names the BSS of the control socket, the first BSS of an AP
MLD, while a non-MLO station has its entry on the link it associated to
alone. hostapd_del_mscs() and hostapd_robust_av_configure() look the
associated station up on every link of the AP MLD and act on the BSS of
its association link. The ubus caller of hostapd_robust_av_configure()
already resolves that BSS with hostapd_ubus_sta_bss().

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
